<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!-- LASSO_CHERRYPICKER_REMOVAL_1. Owner, typed, 2026-10-01: "Remove lasso's from the game, but keep this"
       (the capstan turret). Melee Animation (co.uk.epicguru.meleeanimation) stays installed for its animations.

       Mechanism (bridge5 2026-10-09 A3 FAIL): every Make_AM_Lasso* RecipeDef is an IMPLIED def, generated
       from the ThingDef's <recipeMaker> by the engine's def generator before Cherry Picker runs. Cutting the
       ThingDef in Cherry Picker strips the recipeMaker's recipeUsers but leaves the already-generated RecipeDef
       with its own recipeUsers [ElectricTailoringBench, HandTailoringBench], and the live CP list does not cut
       the RecipeDefs at all. No other installed mod references AM_Lasso* (swept 2026-10-09), so nothing re-adds
       them: the recipe comes from Melee Animation's own recipeMaker.

       Fix at the source: remove <recipeMaker> from the abstract parent AND every child before inheritance and
       implied-def generation, so no lasso recipe is ever generated, whatever the Cherry Picker list says.
       (Removing it from the parent alone would not do: each child carries its own <recipeMaker> holding
       skillRequirements, which still yields a recipe after inheritance.) Spawning on pawns is the mod's C#
       roll, gated by its LassoSpawnChance setting - not reachable from XML; see the item. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Melee Animation</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="AM_LassoBaseMakeable" or @ParentName="AM_LassoBaseMakeable"]/recipeMaker</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
